    "result": "Excellent! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixes Applied\n\n### 1. **Toxicity Metric Signature** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`)\nChanged the function signature from:\n```javascript\nexport function toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)\n```\nto:\n```javascript\nexport function toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)\n```\n\n**Issue**: `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` was interpreting the references array as banned terms, causing false toxicity flags.\n\n### 2. **APPROVAL_STATUSES Export** (`packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`)\nAdded named exports for constants:\n```javascript\nexport {\n  APPROVAL_STATUSES,\n  DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS,\n  GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS,\n  RISK_LEVELS\n};\n```\n\n**Issue**: The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `index.js`, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests pass (8 test files, 0 failures)",
